      "detail": "Robert died at Cardross on 7 June 1329 after a serious illness attested from at least 1327. The traditional account that he suffered from leprosy is disputed by modern historians, who suggest tuberculosis, syphilis or another ailment, and note the leprosy claim may have been English political propaganda.",
